======================================================================
4. VERIFICATION STATUS DEFINITIONS
======================================================================

STATUS V0 — NOT ASSESSED

No verification evidence has currently been identified.

STATUS V1 — DOCUMENTED / REPORTED

A verification result or numerical value is present in recovered
documentation, but the underlying source artifact has not yet been
recovered or linked.

STATUS V2 — EVIDENCE RECOVERED

The underlying computational or source artifact required to assess the
verification item has been recovered.

STATUS V3 — VERIFIED

The underlying artifact has been reviewed and the corresponding
verification criterion has been demonstrated.

STATUS V4 — MANUSCRIPT-LINKED

The verification result is traceable to the numerical dataset and is
appropriate for supporting a manuscript figure, table, or methods claim.

Important:

V1 must not automatically be upgraded to V2.

V2 must not automatically be upgraded to V3.

V3 must not automatically be upgraded to V4.

