21. PROHIBITED VERIFICATION PRACTICES
======================================================================

The following practices are prohibited:

1. Calling a documented numerical value "verified" without evidence.

2. Creating a historical COMSOL solver log that did not actually exist.

3. Creating artificial mesh-convergence results solely to reproduce a
   previously reported percentage.

4. Back-calculating residuals from figure values.

5. Back-calculating energy-balance error from aggregate results.

6. Inferring zero failed elements from a visually acceptable figure.

7. Treating a manuscript figure as equivalent to a native COMSOL solution.

8. Treating the planned six-gravity design as proof that all six gravity
   simulations were executed.

9. Treating patient-level graphical representations as proof of recoverable
   machine-readable numerical output.

10. Changing a previously reported verification value merely to improve
    consistency between tables and figures.

11. Generating missing numerical values from group means.

12. Upgrading a verification status without recording the supporting artifact.

